  "description": "A copy of the r-cat-1-accdb-empty fixture (an empty ACCDB ACE created, 42 pages) opened read/write through DAO. db.Execute CREATE TABLE T (n COUNTER(10, -2), v LONG), then two INSERTs (v = 1, then v = 2), each its own Execute (the second value under a negative increment); then a snapshot SELECT n, v FROM T ORDER BY v reads the issued values. Then Close; pages 0, 1, 2, 3, 7, 8, 10, 17, 18, 41-49 are kept inline and pages 0-49 are hashed. Asks what TDEF bytes 0x14..0x1B hold after inserts when the AutoNumber increment is not 1 (qualified.md R-CAT-1 CAT-X decides them at CREATE only), and which values are issued. Asked for 42cd stretch 4 (the AutoNumber step).",
